Falsifies `jh7110_clock_and_reset::verification::a_transmit_parent_from_the_tree_is_one_of_the_clocks_two_inputs`.

The defect: a parent that is neither of gmac0_tx's two inputs is taken as the mux field value
itself instead of being refused. A tree naming any other clock as the parent would then switch the
mux to an input that does not exist, or one the tree never named.

Expected to fail: the harness's check that an assigned step selects mux input 0 or 1.

